# Manual REST Client requests for GET /people (VS Code REST Client).
# Sign in with any approved review account of REVIEW_ACCOUNTS in apps/backend/.env: set the email and code below.
# Codes are read from the backend log when RESEND_API_KEY is unset.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = admin@example.com
@code = 345678

### Request a sign-in code (expects 202)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "locale": "pt-BR"
}

### Sign in (expects 200 with accessToken)
# @name session
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

###
@token = {{session.response.body.accessToken}}

### Default list: approved users, newest first, 20 per page (expects 200 with { items: [{ id, name, role, createdAt, whatsappNumber }], page, perPage, total })
GET {{baseUrl}}/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter by role and search the name ignoring case and accents (expects 200; "joao" finds "João")
GET {{baseUrl}}/people?role=instructor&search=joao
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sort A–Z by name (expects 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/people?sort=name
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Second page (expects 200; items: [] past the end, with the real total)
GET {{baseUrl}}/people?page=2&perPage=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token (expects 401 auth.token.invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/people

### As a pending, denied, deleted or removed account (expects 403 user.status.notApproved): use that account's token
GET {{baseUrl}}/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid query (expects 422 with errors people.page.invalid, people.perPage.invalid, people.role.invalid, people.sort.invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/people?page=0&perPage=51&role=guest&sort=age
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
